/-!
# Spreading out a stalk subalgebra: the subalgebra `𝒪_X + ℐ · A`

The splitting hypothesis `hsplit` of
`Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.isElementaryChain_of_isAlmostIso` needs an intermediate subalgebra
`𝒪_X ⊊ 𝒜 ⊊ f_*𝒪_{X'}`. At the stalk, `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.addMapMaximalIdeal_ne_top` says
that `𝒪_{X,x} + m_x·(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x` is proper whenever `f` is not an isomorphism at `x`. This file
carries that subalgebra up to the quasi-coherent subalgebra `𝒪_X + ℐ · A`, for an arbitrary
quasi-coherent ideal sheaf `ℐ` and an arbitrary quasi-coherent algebra sheaf `A`.

It is the subalgebra `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.genSubalg` generated
by the ideal-times-module subsheaf `ℐ · A` (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSmul.idealPowSmul`
at `n = 1`). Over an affine open `ℐ(U) · Γ(A, U)` is an ideal of `Γ(A, U)`
(`Ideal.smul_top_eq_map`), hence closed under multiplication, so the subalgebra it generates is
`Γ(X, U) · 1 + ℐ(U) · Γ(A, U)`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.idealSmulModule`: the submodule `ℐ · A` of the underlying module
  of `A`, i.e. `idealPowSmul ℐ 1` of it.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.idealSmulSet`: its sections over an affine open, read as a set of
  sections of `A` — the generating set of the subalgebra.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.idealSmulSubalg`: **the concrete subalgebra `𝒪_X + ℐ · A` of `A`.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.mem_idealSmulSubalg_iff`: **the sections over an affine open.** A
  section of `A` over an affine open `U` lies in the subalgebra exactly when it lies in the
  `Γ(X, U)`-subalgebra of `Γ(A, U)` generated by `ℐ(U) · Γ(A, U)`.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.isQuasicoherent_idealSmulSubalg` and
  `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.isFinite_idealSmulSubalg`: it is quasi-coherent, and — for `A`
  integral with coherent underlying module on a locally Noetherian scheme — **finite**, which
  is what `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_split_isAlmostIso_of_algebraHom` asks of `𝒜`.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.obj_idealSmulSubalg_eq_top`: **where `ℐ` is the unit ideal the
  subalgebra is all of `A`.** So for `ℐ` the ideal sheaf of a closed point `x`, the subalgebra
  differs from `A` only over opens meeting `x`, and its stalk away from `x` is `(f_*𝒪_{X'})_y`.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.ne_top_obj_idealSmulSubalg`: **properness.** For `A = f_*𝒪_{X'}` with
  `f` finite, an affine open `U`, a point `x ∈ U` and `ℐ(U)` inside the prime cut out by `x`,
  the sections of `𝒪_X + ℐ · f_*𝒪_{X'}` over `U` are not all of `Γ(X', f⁻¹U)` as soon as
  `𝒪_{X,x} ≠ (f_*𝒪_{X'})_x`.
* `Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.exists_isFinite_subalg_ne_top`: **the spreading-out.** At a closed
  point where `f` is not an isomorphism there is a finite quasi-coherent subalgebra of
  `f_*𝒪_{X'}` which is proper over an affine open around that point.

## How properness is proved

`ne_top_obj_idealSmulSubalg` is the contrapositive. If the subalgebra had *all* the sections
over `U`, then every section of `Γ(X', f⁻¹U)` would lie in the `Γ(X, U)`-algebra generated by
`ℐ(U)·Γ(X', f⁻¹U)`, and applying the germ at `x` — a ring map — carries that statement to
`(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x = 𝒪_{X,x} + m_x·(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x`, which Nakayama forbids
(`Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.addMapMaximalIdeal_ne_top`). Three facts make the carry work:

* the germ of a section of `ℐ(U)` lands in `m_x`, because the maximal ideal of the stalk pulls
  back along the germ to the prime cut out by `x`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.comap_maximalIdeal_germ`);
* the germ commutes with the structure map, `TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply`, so
  the image of the base ring lands in `𝒪_{X,x}·1`;
* the germ map is *surjective up to denominators*: the stalk of the pushforward along an affine
  morphism is the localisation of `Γ(X', f⁻¹U)` at the image of the prime
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_pushforwardStalk`), and the denominators come
  from `Γ(X, U)`, so their germs are **units of `𝒪_{X,x}`** and the subalgebra
  `𝒪_{X,x} + m_x·(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x` already absorbs their inverses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YD)
-/
@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.RelativeSpec Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSmul

attribute [local instance_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

universe u

namespace Stacks.GlueSquishFactor

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (A : AlgebraSheaf X) [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A]
  (I : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- The submodule `ℐ · A` of the underlying module of `A`. -/
abbrev idealSmulModule : (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A).Submodule :=
  idealPowSmul I 1 (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A)

/-- `ℐ · A` is quasi-coherent, being `I ^ 1 • F` for a quasi-coherent `F`. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_idealSmulModule :
    ((idealSmulModule A I).toSheafOfModules : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent :=
  isQuasicoherent_idealPowSmul I 1 (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A)

/-- The sections of `ℐ · A` over the affine opens form a compatible family, which is the input
`genSubalg` takes. -/
theorem isCompatible_idealSmulModule :
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.IsCompatible (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A)
      fun U : X.affineOpens =>
        Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubmoduleGlueOpens.sections (idealSmulModule A I) U.1 :=
  isCompatible_sections (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A) (idealSmulModule A I)
    (isQuasicoherent_idealSmulModule A I)

/-- **The subalgebra `𝒪_X + ℐ · A`.** -/
def idealSmulSubalg : AlgebraSheaf.Subalg A :=
  genSubalg A (idealSmulModule A I) (isCompatible_idealSmulModule A I)

/-- The sections of `ℐ · A` over an affine open are `ℐ(U) · Γ(A, U)`. -/
theorem sections_idealSmulModule (U : X.affineOpens) :
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SubmoduleGlueOpens.sections (idealSmulModule A I) U.1 =
      I.ideal U • (⊤ : Submodule Γ(X, U.1) Γ(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U.1)) := by
  have h := obj_idealPowSmul I 1 (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A) U
  rw [pow_one] at h
  exact h

/-- The set of sections of `ℐ · A` over an affine open, as a set of sections of `A`. -/
def idealSmulSet (U : X.affineOpens) : Set (AlgebraSheaf.sections A U.1) :=
  ((I.ideal U • (⊤ : Submodule Γ(X, U.1) Γ(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U.1)) :
    Submodule Γ(X, U.1) Γ(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U.1)) :
      Set Γ(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U.1))

/-- `sections_idealSmulModule` read as an equality of generating sets. -/
theorem submoduleSet_idealSmulModule (U : X.affineOpens) :
    submoduleSet A (idealSmulModule A I) U.1 = idealSmulSet A I U :=
  congrArg _ (sections_idealSmulModule A I U)

/-- The affine-local family `genSubalg` is built from is, for `ℐ · A`, the subalgebra generated
by `ℐ(U) · Γ(A, U)`. -/
theorem genFamily_idealSmulModule (U : X.affineOpens) :
    genFamily A (idealSmulModule A I) U = adjoinSubmodule A U.1 (idealSmulSet A I U) :=
  congrArg (adjoinSubmodule A U.1) (submoduleSet_idealSmulModule A I U)

/-- **The sections of `𝒪_X + ℐ · A` over an affine open.** A section lies in the subalgebra
exactly when it lies in the `Γ(X, U)`-subalgebra of `Γ(A, U)` generated by `ℐ(U) · Γ(A, U)`;
since that set is an ideal of `Γ(A, U)`, the subalgebra is `Γ(X, U) · 1 + ℐ(U) · Γ(A, U)`. -/
theorem mem_idealSmulSubalg_iff (U : X.affineOpens) (x : AlgebraSheaf.sections A U.1) :
    x ∈ (idealSmulSubalg A I).obj U.1 ↔ x ∈ adjoinSubmodule A U.1 (idealSmulSet A I U) :=
  (mem_genSubalg_obj_iff A (idealSmulModule A I) (isCompatible_idealSmulModule A I) U x).trans
    (genFamily_idealSmulModule A I U ▸ Iff.rfl)

omit [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A] in
/-- On an affine open where `ℐ` is the unit ideal the generating set is everything. -/
theorem idealSmulSet_eq_univ {U : X.affineOpens} (hU : I.ideal U = ⊤) :
    idealSmulSet A I U = Set.univ := by
  change ((I.ideal U • (⊤ : Submodule Γ(X, U.1) Γ(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U.1)) :
    Submodule Γ(X, U.1) Γ(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U.1)) :
      Set Γ(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A, U.1)) = Set.univ
  rw [hU, Submodule.top_smul, Submodule.top_coe]

/-- **Where `ℐ` is the unit ideal, `𝒪_X + ℐ · A` is all of `A`.** For `ℐ` the ideal sheaf of a
closed point this says the subalgebra differs from `A` only over the opens meeting that point. -/
theorem obj_idealSmulSubalg_eq_top {V : X.Opens}
    (hV : ∀ W : X.affineOpens, W.1 ≤ V → I.ideal W = ⊤) :
    (idealSmulSubalg A I).obj V = ⊤ := by
  refine top_unique fun x _ => ?_
  change ∀ (W : X.affineOpens) (hW : W.1 ≤ V),
    (A.right.obj.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom x ∈ genFamily A (idealSmulModule A I) W
  intro W hW
  rw [genFamily_idealSmulModule, idealSmulSet_eq_univ A I (hV W hW)]
  let := AlgebraSheaf.algebraSections A W.1
  change _ ∈ Subalgebra.toSubmodule
    (Algebra.adjoin Γ(X, W.1) (Set.univ : Set (AlgebraSheaf.sections A W.1)))
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_univ]
  trivial

/-- **`𝒪_X + ℐ · A` is quasi-coherent**, by `isQuasicoherent_genSubalg`. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_idealSmulSubalg :
    (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf (idealSmulSubalg A I)).IsQuasicoherent :=
  isQuasicoherent_genSubalg A (idealSmulModule A I) (isCompatible_idealSmulModule A I)

/-- **`𝒪_X + ℐ · A` is finite.** On a locally Noetherian scheme `ℐ · A` is a quasi-coherent
submodule of a coherent module, hence coherent, hence of finite type; the subalgebra it
generates is then finite over an integral `A` by `isFinite_genSubalg`. -/
theorem isFinite_idealSmulSubalg [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (hAint : A.IsIntegral)
    [(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A : X.Modules).IsCoherent] :
    (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf (idealSmulSubalg A I)).IsFinite :=
  isFinite_genSubalg A hAint (idealSmulModule A I) (isCompatible_idealSmulModule A I)
    (isQuasicoherent_idealSmulModule A I)
    (isCoherent_idealPowSmul I 1 (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule A)).isFiniteType

/-! ### Properness over an affine open around a point -/

/-- A section over an affine open lies in the prime cut out by `x` iff its germ at `x` lies in
the maximal ideal of the stalk. -/
private theorem mem_primeIdealOf_iff_germ_mem_maximalIdeal {X : Scheme.{u}} {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U) (r : Γ(X, U)) :
    r ∈ (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal ↔
      X.presheaf.germ U x hx r ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  rw [← IsAffineOpen.comap_maximalIdeal_germ hU (⟨x, hx⟩ : U), Ideal.mem_comap]

/-- **Germs of sections of `𝒪_X + ℐ · f_*𝒪_{X'}`.** If `ℐ(U)` lies in the prime cut out by
`x ∈ U`, the germ at `x` of a section of `𝒪_X + ℐ · f_*𝒪_{X'}` over the affine open `U` lies in
`𝒪_{X,x} + m_x·(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x`. -/
theorem germ_mem_addMapMaximalIdeal_of_mem_idealSmulSubalg {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent (pushforwardAlgebra f)] (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (hI : I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ ≤ (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal) (b : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U))
    (hb : b ∈ (idealSmulSubalg (pushforwardAlgebra f) I).obj U) :
    letI : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
      ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
    ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).germ U x hx).hom b ∈
      addMapMaximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) := by
  let : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
    ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
  let := AlgebraSheaf.algebraSections (pushforwardAlgebra f) U
  let : Algebra Γ(X, U) Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) := (f.app U).hom.toAlgebra
  change ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).germ U x hx).hom b ∈
    addMapMaximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x)
  have hJ : (I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩).map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) ≤
      Ideal.comap ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).germ U x hx).hom
        ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)).map
          (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x))) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro p hp
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_comap,
      show algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) p = (f.app U).hom p from rfl,
      ← TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply U x hx f.c p]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _
      ((mem_primeIdealOf_iff_germ_mem_maximalIdeal hU hx p).mp (hI hp))
  replace hb : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin Γ(X, U)
      (idealSmulSet (pushforwardAlgebra f) I ⟨U, hU⟩) :=
    (mem_idealSmulSubalg_iff (pushforwardAlgebra f) I ⟨U, hU⟩ b).mp hb
  induction hb using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    refine ⟨0, ?_⟩
    rw [map_zero, sub_zero]
    refine hJ ?_
    have h1 : y ∈ I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ • (⊤ : Submodule Γ(X, U) Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) := hy
    rwa [Ideal.smul_top_eq_map] at h1
  | algebraMap r =>
    refine ⟨X.presheaf.germ U x hx r, ?_⟩
    convert Ideal.zero_mem _ using 1
    exact sub_eq_zero.mpr (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply U x hx f.c r).symm
  | add y z hy hz py pz =>
    rw [map_add]
    exact add_mem py pz
  | mul y z hy hz py pz =>
    rw [map_mul]
    exact mul_mem py pz

/-- **From germs to the whole stalk.** For `f` affine and `x` in an affine open `U`, if the germ
at `x` of every section of `f_*𝒪_{X'}` over `U` lies in `𝒪_{X,x} + m_x·(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x`, then so
does every element of the stalk `(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x`: the stalk is the localisation of
`Γ(X', f⁻¹U)` at the prime cut out by `x`, and the germs of the denominators are units of
`𝒪_{X,x}`. -/
theorem mem_addMapMaximalIdeal_of_forall_germ_mem {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    [IsAffineHom f] {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (h : letI : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
        ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
      ∀ b : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U), ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).germ U x hx).hom b ∈
        addMapMaximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x))
    (b' : (f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :
    letI : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
      ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
    b' ∈ addMapMaximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) := by
  let : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
    ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
  let : Algebra Γ(X, U) Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) := (f.app U).hom.toAlgebra
  let : Algebra Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
    ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).germ U x hx).hom.toAlgebra
  change b' ∈ addMapMaximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x)
  replace h : ∀ b : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U), ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).germ U x hx).hom b ∈
      addMapMaximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) := h
  have hloc : IsLocalization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)
      (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
    IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_pushforwardStalk f hU hx
  obtain ⟨⟨b, sden⟩, hbs⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl) b'
  obtain ⟨r, hr, hrs⟩ := sden.2
  have hrp : r ∉ (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal := hr
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ : IsUnit (X.presheaf.germ U x hx r) :=
    IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.mp fun hcon =>
      hrp ((mem_primeIdealOf_iff_germ_mem_maximalIdeal hU hx r).mpr hcon)
  have hsden : algebraMap Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) (sden : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U))
      = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x)
        (X.presheaf.germ U x hx r) := by
    rw [← hrs, show algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) r = (f.app U).hom r from rfl]
    exact (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply U x hx f.c r).symm
  have hb' : b' = algebraMap Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) b *
      algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) ↑v⁻¹ := by
    have h1 : b' * algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x)
        (X.presheaf.germ U x hx r) =
        algebraMap Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) b := by
      rw [← hsden]
      exact hbs
    rw [← h1, mul_assoc, ← map_mul, ← hv, Units.mul_inv, map_one, mul_one]
  rw [hb']
  exact mul_mem (h b) (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ _)

/-- **Properness of `𝒪_X + ℐ · f_*𝒪_{X'}`.** Let `f : X' ⟶ X` be finite, let `U` be an affine
open, let `x ∈ U` and let `ℐ` be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf whose ideal on `U` is contained in
the prime of `Γ(X, U)` cut out by `x` — for `ℐ` the ideal sheaf of a closed subset containing
`x` this is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSmul.mem_closed_iff_vanishingIdeal_le`. If `f`
is not an isomorphism at `x`, in the form `𝒪_{X,x} ≠ (f_*𝒪_{X'})_x`, then the sections of
`𝒪_X + ℐ · f_*𝒪_{X'}` over `U` are **not** all of `Γ(X', f⁻¹U)`.

If the subalgebra were everything over `U`, the germs at `x` would force
`𝒪_{X,x} + m_x·(f_*𝒪_{X'})_x` to be the whole stalk, which Nakayama forbids
(`Stacks.GlueSquishFactor.addMapMaximalIdeal_ne_top`). -/
theorem ne_top_obj_idealSmulSubalg {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) [IsFinite f]
    [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent (pushforwardAlgebra f)] (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (hI : I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ ≤ (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal)
    (hne : letI : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
        ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
      (⊥ : Subalgebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x)) ≠ ⊤) :
    (idealSmulSubalg (pushforwardAlgebra f) I).obj U ≠ ⊤ := by
  let : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
    ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
    module_finite_stalk_pushforward f x
  intro htop
  exact addMapMaximalIdeal_ne_top (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) hne
    (top_unique fun b' _ =>
      mem_addMapMaximalIdeal_of_forall_germ_mem f hU hx (fun b =>
        germ_mem_addMapMaximalIdeal_of_mem_idealSmulSubalg f I hU hx hI b
          (htop ▸ Subring.mem_top b)) b')

/-- **The spreading-out of [Stacks, Tag 0C1L].** Let `f : X' ⟶ X` be a finite morphism to a
locally Noetherian scheme whose pushforward algebra is quasi-coherent with coherent underlying
module, let `x` be a closed point lying in an affine open `U`, and suppose `f` is not an
isomorphism at `x`. Then there is a **finite quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-subalgebra of `f_*𝒪_{X'}`
which is proper over `U`**, namely `𝒪_X + ℐ_x · f_*𝒪_{X'}` for `ℐ_x` the ideal sheaf of the
reduced point. -/
theorem exists_isFinite_subalg_ne_top {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) [IsFinite f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent (pushforwardAlgebra f)]
    [(AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule (pushforwardAlgebra f) : X.Modules).IsCoherent]
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U) (hcl : IsClosed ({x} : Set X))
    (hne : letI : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x) :=
        ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} x).map f.c).hom.toAlgebra
      (⊥ : Subalgebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) ((f.base _* X'.presheaf).stalk x)) ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ C : AlgebraSheaf.Subalg (pushforwardAlgebra f),
      (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf C).IsQuasicoherent ∧
        (AlgebraSheaf.Subalg.toAlgebraSheaf C).IsFinite ∧ C.obj U ≠ ⊤ :=
  ⟨idealSmulSubalg (pushforwardAlgebra f) (closedIdeal ⟨{x}, hcl⟩),
    isQuasicoherent_idealSmulSubalg _ _,
    isFinite_idealSmulSubalg _ _ (AlgebraicGeometry.isFinite_pushforwardAlgebra f).isIntegral,
    ne_top_obj_idealSmulSubalg f _ hU hx
      ((mem_closed_iff_vanishingIdeal_le ⟨{x}, hcl⟩ ⟨U, hU⟩ x hx).mp rfl) hne⟩

end Stacks.GlueSquishFactor

